# ADVERSARIAL FIXTURE — a source that tries to break OUT of the artifact's
# own metadata block.
#
# Core §7 makes every artifact self-carrying: the renderer embeds the FULL
# SOURCE TEXT in `<metadata id="figdown-source">`, inside a CDATA section,
# beside a SHA-256 of that source. Embedding a document inside a document is
# exactly the shape that injection attacks are made of, and CDATA has one
# terminator — `]]>` — so a source containing `]]>` is the attack.
#
# THIS FILE CONTAINS THAT TERMINATOR, in a comment and in a string, together
# with the pre-spliced form an attacker would reach for next
# (`]]]]><![CDATA[>`), a closing `</metadata>` tag, and a `<script>` element
# positioned to run if any of them landed. Here is the terminator, in this
# comment, unquoted: ]]>
# And the pre-spliced form, which must not be un-spliced back into one: ]]]]><![CDATA[>
# And a closing tag with a script behind it: </metadata><script>alert(1)</script>
#
# WHAT THIS FIXTURE PINS. The `.model.json` golden pins only the ordinary
# part: the document parses, and comments are not model content. The real
# assertion is `gate:safesvg`'s, and it is a ROUNDTRIP one — render this file
# to an artifact, read the artifact as XML, and require that
#
#   1. the text recovered from `<metadata id="figdown-source">` equals these
#      bytes exactly, so the splice is reversible and the embedded source is
#      still the source; and
#   2. `data-sha256` equals the SHA-256 of these bytes, so the escaping did
#      not change what the hash covers; and
#   3. no `<script>` element exists anywhere in the parsed tree, so nothing
#      above escaped the CDATA section.
#
# A NOTE FOR CONSUMERS, because this fixture is what proves the point: an
# extractor that finds the source with a non-greedy regex up to the first
# `</metadata>` gets the WRONG ANSWER on this file — it stops inside the
# CDATA, at the closing tag written in the comment three lines up. Recovering
# the embedded source requires an extractor that knows where CDATA sections
# begin and end. The engine's escaping is correct; a careless reader of it
# need not be.
figdown 0.3 block
title "]]> </metadata> <![CDATA[ <script>alert(1)</script>"
node a "]]]]><![CDATA[>" note="]]>"
node b "<![CDATA[ unterminated"
edge a -> b
